WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.840 --> 00:00:05.360
A warm welcome to Noomi Rapace.

00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:24.960
Welcome!
It's hard to believe you're here.

00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:30.000
I read about you in the papers,
and you're hugely productive.

00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:36.280
-Do you have a clear grasp of it all?
-No.

00:00:36.440 --> 00:00:41.600
I forget which country I'm in,
I mix up languages, and I feel...

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:48.680
I lose the outer structure,
but my inner radar is pretty clear.

00:00:48.840 --> 00:00:53.440
-You're in Stockholm, just FYI.
-Right, I landed today.

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:57.560
You're here for the movie premiere
of "The Drop".

00:00:57.720 --> 00:01:02.600
We'll see a clip from that later,
but you're also making another film?

00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:08.600
No, we finished a week ago.
I injured my foot, so my walk is wonky.

00:01:08.760 --> 00:01:13.840
-You picked the right shoes, then.
-I know.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:17.640
-What happened?
-Painkillers.

00:01:17.800 --> 00:01:23.160
No, I jumped...
On the last night of shooting...

00:01:23.320 --> 00:01:28.280
It's like a female Bourne,
and I play a CIA agent.

00:01:28.440 --> 00:01:32.280
-Jason Bourne, but female. Wow!
-Right.

00:01:32.440 --> 00:01:36.560
So I run, shoot, fight,
and survive a lot-

00:01:36.720 --> 00:01:43.400
-while trying to save people
for about two hours or so.

00:01:43.560 --> 00:01:49.240
On the last night, I jumped out a window
while escaping this house-

00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:53.680
-and I'm supposed to jump this fence
in heels.

00:01:53.840 --> 00:01:59.000
I landed on the foot and something
happened to the ball of my foot.

00:01:59.160 --> 00:02:02.760
I've been partly disabled for a week.

00:02:02.920 --> 00:02:07.240
And for the film, "The Drop",
what did you have to do?

00:02:08.720 --> 00:02:15.480
Well, I went to strip clubs in New York
for research.

00:02:15.640 --> 00:02:19.400
What? I've seen the film;
there are no strip clubs.

00:02:19.560 --> 00:02:23.240
No, it's more to do with her back story.

00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:28.840
If there are any omissions or gaps,
I have to...

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:32.800
If there's a pause in a scene,
I need to fill it.

00:02:32.960 --> 00:02:37.200
"What is she thinking,
what has she gone through?"

00:02:37.360 --> 00:02:42.080
In order to build a back story,
sometimes I have to do research.

00:02:42.240 --> 00:02:48.800
I think that she... In one scene,
we find out she wanted to be a dancer-

00:02:48.960 --> 00:02:53.720
-but it didn't work out, so I think
she started stripping instead.

00:02:53.880 --> 00:02:59.160
I talked to the director, and he agreed.
So I did research in strip clubs-

00:02:59.320 --> 00:03:05.560
-and at a rescue center for dogs.
So it was dogs and naked women...

00:03:05.720 --> 00:03:12.480
I met you not too long ago, by chance,
in a bar in London.

00:03:12.640 --> 00:03:19.240
And I was... I really felt
how old I've become.

00:03:19.400 --> 00:03:26.120
I was heading out to go to bed,
and I felt like the most boring person.

00:03:26.280 --> 00:03:31.800
You had your little umbrella,
and you looked like a little old man.

00:03:31.960 --> 00:03:35.960
I really did! I saw myself
the way you saw me.

00:03:36.120 --> 00:03:40.240
-I wanted to be more...
-I think we were just heading out.

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:44.720
-The night had just started for you.
-Right, right.

00:03:44.880 --> 00:03:48.320
And I just went in and then to bed.

00:03:48.480 --> 00:03:55.240
I was thinking about you, and you're
so energetic. Are you also restless?

00:03:55.400 --> 00:03:59.440
-Is that always a good thing?
-No.

00:03:59.600 --> 00:04:03.040
It depends on what you do with it.

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:09.880
I've found a way to channel my energy
and my pace.

00:04:10.040 --> 00:04:16.240
It can get rather messy if you're
out of sync with everyone else-

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:21.440
-and I have been in the past.
I got started as others finished-

00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:27.200
-got tired, or didn't want to work more.
When I was younger-

00:04:27.360 --> 00:04:31.720
-I had always just started
when others were ready to finish.

00:04:31.880 --> 00:04:36.320
That can make you feel lonely
or sort of...

00:04:36.480 --> 00:04:42.880
You can end up out of step
if you don't find a release.

00:04:43.040 --> 00:04:47.920
To me, acting is the perfect...

00:04:48.080 --> 00:04:51.800
It's the perfect channel
to get it all out.

00:04:51.960 --> 00:04:57.360
Now that we filmed "Unlocked",
I get up to work out in the mornings-

00:04:57.520 --> 00:05:02.480
-no matter how early the call time is,
even if it's 4 or 5 AM.

00:05:02.640 --> 00:05:08.480
We shoot throughout the day,
and I work out in the evening again.

00:05:08.640 --> 00:05:15.480
-Then I can sleep well.
-Is there an escape in all of this?

00:05:15.640 --> 00:05:19.840
Absolutely, I think so.
I find it hard to stop.

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:24.240
And I find it scary to have...

00:05:24.400 --> 00:05:30.440
...a day without any plans, but I don't
remember when I had one last.

00:05:30.600 --> 00:05:35.400
But for the first time in my life,
I actually long for it now.

00:05:35.560 --> 00:05:40.240
I actually long for
a time without any plans.

00:05:40.400 --> 00:05:45.720
To be able to wake up and take the days,
or weeks even, as they come.

00:05:45.880 --> 00:05:50.000
I don't think I've ever
longed for that before.

00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:55.960
When you're successful,
people often ask how it has changed you.

00:05:56.120 --> 00:06:02.680
Most say, "not at all, I'm the same".
But I'll ask - has it changed you?

00:06:04.200 --> 00:06:07.320
Has it changed you, somehow?

